      "code": "",
      "note": "The flexible `attr->argv[]` storage is allocated from raw `pemalloc()` memory and vulnerable code does not initialize each slot to `IS_UNDEF` before later population and cleanup. Because the attribute is inserted into the attribute hash before all arguments are compiled, any fatal error during argument compilation leaves trailing `argv[]` slots uninitialized but still subject to destruction. The fix adds a loop that applies `ZVAL_UNDEF(&attr->argv[i])` for every declared argument.",
